17 orcausesavehicletobedrivenrecklessly,asdefinedinRSA626:2,II(c),orsothatthelivesorsafety
18 of the public shall be endangered, or upon a bet, wager, or race, or who drives a vehicle for the
19 purpose of making a record, or who drives a vehicle at a speed of 100 miles per hour or greater, and
20 thereby violates any of the provisions of this title or any rules adopted by the director, shall be,
21 notwithstanding the provisions of title LXII, guilty of a violation and fined not less than $500 plus
22 penalty assessment for the first offense and $750 plus penalty assessment for the second offense nor
23 more than $1,000 plus penalty assessment and his or her license or operating privilege shall be
24 revoked for a period of 60 days for the first offense and from 60 days to one year for the second
